## 2. Executive Summary

The discussion centered on transitioning KDPS's manual, Excel-heavy warehouse operations into an automated, error-free workflow. The main focus areas were optimizing the **Stock Inwarding** pipeline, mitigating **OCR text-reading limitations** caused by faint dot-matrix invoices, and automating **dynamic margin calculations**.

A significant portion of the meeting was dedicated to organizational security—specifically enforcing a **"Maker-vs-Checker" protocol** to prevent a single user from both entering and approving stock data. Furthermore, the technical architecture was discussed regarding using highly accurate LLM APIs (like Claude) to parse inconsistent vendor data structures (such as varying size formats) into a uniform digital "PT File" format before it is transmitted to the Patna central system for automated barcode generation.

